<title>POLAND: Poland invites bids for bicycle maker Romet.</title>
<headline>Poland invites bids for bicycle maker Romet.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish treasury ministry is inviting bids for up to 80 percent of the shares of bicycle maker Zaklady Rowerowe Romet SA, the ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said in a newspaper advertisement that investors could place offers for at least 10 percent of shares in the company by April 7.</p>
<p>It said 15 percent of shares in the company would be earmarked for employees and five percent for restitution claims.</p>
<p>The company, based in the central city of Bydgoszcz, employs 4,000 people.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
